;; The models `/model` offers, most useful first — brainyard's curated entries
;; (`clj-llm/core/providers.clj` `model-catalog`, the ones with a
;; `:curated-rank`, in rank order), for the providers this port can reach.
;; google, deepseek, mistral, groq and apple-fm are left out: the port has no
;; provider for them (RFC-006).
;;
;; A RESOURCE, not code (RFC-001): which models are worth offering changes
;; when a vendor ships one, and saying so should not need a rebuild. Nothing
;; here limits what `/model provider/model` accepts — any model a provider
;; serves can be named; this is only what the picker lists.
;;
;; Ahead of brainyard's list (divergence `models-ahead-of-brainyard`): the
;; Claude 5.5 and 5.1 models, each above the one it succeeds, ids from
;; platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/overview, checked
;; 2026-10-09 (byj-gly.323).
;;
;; `:light? true` marks the one model per provider that light-tier side tasks
;; (the recap, command rephrasing) run on when `:agent-lm-tiers` names none —
;; the session's provider's, so they bill the account the session does
;; (byj-gly.367, RFC-005 "The light tier"). A provider with none marked runs
;; them on the session's model.
;;
;; `:model` is the provider's own id; `/model` switches to
;; `provider/model`, and a bare `:model` (`/model sonnet`) finds its entry here.
